{"tool_name":"bioconductor-tomoda","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"bioconductor-tomoda","identifiers":["doi:10.18129/b9.bioc.tomoda"],"license":"Not available","summary":"Tomo-seq data analysis","home_url":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.12/bioc/html/tomoda.html","keywords":["Clustering","RNA-Seq","Transcriptomics"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":119},"biotools":{"id":"bioconductor-tomoda","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/tomoda","license":"MIT","summary":"This package provides many easy-to-use methods to analyze and visualize tomo-seq data. The tomo-seq technique is based on cryosectioning of tissue and performing RNA-seq on consecutive sections. (Reference: Kruse F, Junker JP, van Oudenaarden A, Bakkers J. Tomo-seq: A method to obtain genome-wide expression data with spatial resolution. Methods Cell Biol. 2016;135:299-307. doi:10.1016/bs.mcb.2016.01.006) The main purpose of the package is to find zones with similar transcriptional profiles and spatially expressed genes in a tomo-seq sample. Several visulization functions are available to create easy-to-modify plots.","addition_date":"2026-08-30T02:54:21.055933Z","last_update_date":"2026-08-30T02:54:21.057973Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.22.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:bioconductor-tomoda","credit":[{"name":"Wendao Liu","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer","Maintainer"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/tomoda"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"name":"tomoda","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"gh2biotools","publication":[{"doi":"10.18129/B9.bioc.tomoda"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"tomoda","home":"https://bio.tools/bioconductor-tomoda","license":"MIT","version":"1.22.0","summary":"This package provides many easy-to-use methods to analyze and visualize tomo-seq data. The tomo-seq techn